{"data": [{"id": "2122107602805063718", "author_id": "2043615144639393792", "text": "@testingcatalog Splitting models by role makes a lot of sense cost-wise: a strong model for the coordinator that plans, and a cheaper fast one for threads doing routine edits. Curious whether the coordinator can switch a thread's model mid-task when it gets stuck.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:20:54.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/Daeman_771/status/2122107602805063718", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122098385088086282", "author_id": "990697855", "text": "@testingcatalog \"you can now\" bro i've had this shit for a month or more", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:44:16.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/notiyda/status/2122098385088086282", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 29, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122082993128747446", "author_id": "2120992973806501889", "text": "@testingcatalog Big planner, small workers. Curious which combo people settle on.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:43:06.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/WYZBen87/status/2122082993128747446", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122081789019668598", "author_id": "1802300156550721536", "text": "@testingcatalog Smart model as the boss, cheaper one doing the work. Just like a real company", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:38:19.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/iambokensha/status/2122081789019668598", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122078488320491832", "author_id": "1352015106515869698", "text": "@testingcatalog Model per role is the right knob. I run 18 jobs in my business on Claude managed agents with Haiku 5.5 doing the writing. On 30 judged test cases the setup routed 28 correctly with zero wrong sends, so cheap on the worker side holds up.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:25:12.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/IncomeSurfers/status/2122078488320491832", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122075990205882467", "author_id": "2849761194", "text": "@testingcatalog Id love to use projects. But they are tied to a cloud environment and account right? If I used multiple Claude subscriptions, I wouldn’t be able to share the project?", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:15:16.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/android_stern/status/2122075990205882467", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 44, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122073821867917526", "author_id": "1291813544", "text": "@testingcatalog Separate models per role is the setting I wanted most.\nA cheap one for routine checks and the heavy one only for hard bugs would cut my usage a lot.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:06:40.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/livesanches/status/2122073821867917526", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122069485783769504", "author_id": "2038912785631920128", "text": "@testingcatalog I really like that, since the coordinator is where I want a frontier model, and most of the threads can run on something much cheaper.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T20:49:26.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/samaschke/status/2122069485783769504", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122055649894773007", "author_id": "1648468797874110465", "text": "@testingcatalog Thanks a lot, that makes more sense now. So it’s really about getting the project’s system prompt right. It’s a bit of a shift when you’re used to working with regular sessions. I feel like it would’ve been simpler if we could just set a goal for the coordinator itself.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:54:27.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/apinataya/status/2122055649894773007", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122048873892126734", "author_id": "2054501072966684672", "text": "@testingcatalog Cheaper thread models may lower the bill at fixed fan-out, but spending the savings on more threads also grows the coordinator's context.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:27:31.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/TinyRouterHQ/status/2122048873892126734", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122047252910985678", "author_id": "2081866937164795905", "text": "@testingcatalog If you change the coordinator model halfway through a project, do existing threads keep their original model? That detail matters when comparing two runs of the same task.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:21:05.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/almosttomorrowe/status/2122047252910985678", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122046836718322166", "author_id": "445958841", "text": "@testingcatalog The Coordinator now proactively updates you across every thread without being asked. Took me three performance cycles to get that out of actual humans, and even then only during review season.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:19:26.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/CatKingAC/status/2122046836718322166", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122046612297920828", "author_id": "2122009674673278976", "text": "@testingcatalog the obvious play here: put your strongest model on the coordinator doing the planning and checking, and a cheaper, faster one on the threads doing the grunt work. stretches your limits further.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:18:32.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/theplaintake/status/2122046612297920828", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122046214111986141", "author_id": "2119364194780708864", "text": "@testingcatalog use claude code every night and i've never opened projects once lol. is this new or am i just late", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:16:57.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/KysonBuilds/status/2122046214111986141", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122045308133851518", "author_id": "3980735590", "text": "@apinataya in Projects, the goal belongs to the project itself (you set it in Project settings &gt; General), and the coordinator hands out the work. So a per-session /goal would compete with it.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:13:21.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/testingcatalog/status/2122045308133851518", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 355, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "2043615144639393792", "username": "Daeman_771", "name": "ilsanjibuzang", "verified": false}, {"id": "3980735590", "username": "testingcatalog", "name": "🚨 AI News | TestingCatalog", "verified": true}, {"id": "990697855", "username": "notiyda", "name": "iyda", "verified": false}, {"id": "2120992973806501889", "username": "WYZBen87", "name": "Ben", "verified": false}, {"id": "1802300156550721536", "username": "iambokensha", "name": "bokensha", "verified": false}, {"id": "1352015106515869698", "username": "IncomeSurfers", "name": "Income Stream Surfers", "verified": false}, {"id": "2849761194", "username": "android_stern", "name": "Andrew", "verified": false}, {"id": "1291813544", "username": "livesanches", "name": "Felipe Sanches", "verified": false}, {"id": "2038912785631920128", "username": "samaschke", "name": "Karsten Samaschke", "verified": false}, {"id": "1648468797874110465", "username": "apinataya", "name": "Apina d'Taya - 🌍", "verified": false}, {"id": "2054501072966684672", "username": "TinyRouterHQ", "name": "TinyRouter", "verified": false}, {"id": "2081866937164795905", "username": "almosttomorrowe", "name": "Almost Tomorrow", "verified": false}, {"id": "445958841", "username": "CatKingAC", "name": "CatKingAC", "verified": false}, {"id": "2122009674673278976", "username": "theplaintake", "name": "The Plain Take", "verified": false}, {"id": "2119364194780708864", "username": "KysonBuilds", "name": "Kyson", "verified": false}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2122107602805063718", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzow692gcy75vfw80nw7joblj06f1", "oldest_id": "2122045308133851518", "result_count": 15}}